WEBVTT

00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:02.180
A gorilla walked right past them.

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:05.759
In a famous 1999 study, people watched

00:00:05.769 --> 00:00:09.084
two teams pass basketballs,
and counted one

00:00:09.094 --> 00:00:10.494
team's passes.

00:00:10.504 --> 00:00:12.606
Then a person in a gorilla suit

00:00:12.616 --> 00:00:14.344
strolled right through the middle of the

00:00:14.354 --> 00:00:15.124
game.

00:00:15.134 --> 00:00:17.512
About half of the viewers never noticed

00:00:17.522 --> 00:00:18.050
it.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.950
So researchers tested
experts who search images

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:22.160
for a living:

00:00:22.185 --> 00:00:26.175
radiologists, hunting lung
scans for tiny cancer

00:00:26.185 --> 00:00:27.183
nodules.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.927
Into one scan, they slipped a gorilla,

00:00:29.952 --> 00:00:32.301
far bigger than any of the nodules.

00:00:32.311 --> 00:00:35.342
Eighty-three percent of the
radiologists missed it.

00:00:35.352 --> 00:00:37.977
And eye-tracking showed most of those who

00:00:37.987 --> 00:00:39.925
missed it had looked right at it.
